1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,620
Do you like somewhere a little bit different to the usual types of places you find on the high street?
你喜欢那些与你在商业街常见的地方稍微不同的地方吗？

2
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:11,410
I do, so I'm glad to see new ones popping up everywhere in London.
我喜欢，所以我很高兴看到伦敦到处都涌现这类新地方。

3
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:14,950
The so called pop-up shop is a temporary arrangement.
所谓的快闪店是一种临时的商业形式。

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:21,590
In the aftermath of the financial crisis of 2008, many businesses had to shut down.
在2008年金融危机之后，许多企业不得不倒闭。

5
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:26,530
Shops, warehouses and offices were left vacant when they stopped trading.
商店、仓库和办公室在停止营业后都被空置了出来。

6
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:30,160
Pop-up entrepreneurs occupied some of them quickly.
快闪店的创业者们迅速占据了其中一些地方。

7
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:38,190
For them the appeal of this temporary shopping concept is clear: they can start a business with much lower risk.
对他们来说，这种临时购物概念的吸引力很明显：他们可以以低得多的风险开展业务。

8
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:47,940
The temporary nature of a pop-up gives the opportunity to test a product and develop a customer base, without being tied in to a long-term renting contract.
快闪店的临时性提供了一个测试产品和发展客户基础的机会，而且无需受限于长期租赁合同。

9
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:54,330
Being small makes it much easier for pop-ups to expand if they are successful.
规模小使得快闪店如果经营成功，扩展起来会容易得多。

10
00:00:54,330 --> 00:01:01,240
Pop-up shops first appeared in the UK in the early 2000s, with the economy booming.
快闪店最早在21世纪初英国经济繁荣的时候出现。

11
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:08,270
They were originally a way for small, niche companies to rent retail space in great locations.
它们最初是小型的、针对特定小众市场的公司在黄金地段租赁零售空间的一种方式。

12
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:12,990
This was while landlords who owned these spaces looked for permanent tenants.
与此同时，拥有这些空间的房东则在寻找长期租户。

13
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:16,470
Pop-up shops can take a number of different forms.
快闪店可以有许多不同的形式。

14
00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:20,610
They might be temporary shops in the high street or a shopping centre.
它们可能是商业街或购物中心里的临时店铺。

15
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:23,280
They might be simple market stalls.
也可能是简单的市场摊位。

16
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:27,230
They could be based in some kind of transport, like a food truck.
它们还可能基于某种交通工具，比如餐车。

17
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:35,650
Or they could be run by people who visit different establishments, like travelling chefs who take over pub and restaurant kitchens temporarily.
或者它们可能由那些会前往不同企业的人来经营，比如临时接管酒吧和餐馆厨房的巡回厨师。

18
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:50,030
According to a 2014 report by the Centre of Economic and Business Research, the pop-up industry was worth £2.1bn and is expected to grow by 8.4% this year.
根据经济与商业研究中心2014年的一份报告，快闪店行业价值21亿英镑，预计今年将增长8.4%。

19
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:54,630
Almost anything that can be on a high street can also be a pop-up.
几乎任何能出现在商业街上的业态都可以成为快闪店的形式。

20
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:59,710
There have been pop-up shops, art galleries, theatres and restaurants among others.
已经出现过快闪商店、艺术画廊、剧院和餐馆等等。

21
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:04,720
In an age of fast-changing habits, the pop-up idea might be here to stay.
在一个习惯快速变化的时代，快闪店的概念可能会一直存在下去。
